# Full environment variable reference: see ENV_VARS.md
# This file only shows examples for common settings.

# Pick one or more providers, or set DEEPAGENTS_MODEL explicitly.

# OpenAI (GPT-4, best general capability, paid per token)
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Cursor (editor-integrated, proprietary, paid; requires CURSOR_BASE_URL)
CURSOR_API_KEY=

# Google Gemini (free tier available, good for testing; set GOOGLE_API_KEY)
GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# Anthropic Claude (paid, strong reasoning; requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Ollama (local-only, keyless, requires host daemon; set OLLAMA_HOST=http://host.docker.internal:11434)
OLLAMA_API_KEY=

# LM Studio (local-only, keyless; requires LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL)
LMSTUDIO_API_KEY=

# Ollama (local, keyless) -- now the DEFAULT provider (priority 0), so this
# matters for a stock run, not just an opt-in one.
# Inside the container `localhost` is the container, not
# the host, so a host-run Ollama daemon is unreachable by default. run-docker maps
# `host.docker.internal` to the host (on Linux via --add-host=host-gateway), so
# point OLLAMA_HOST at it. Keep this COMMENTED OUT unless you set a value: an empty
# `OLLAMA_HOST=` is passed through as an empty string and breaks the client default
# (which falls back to localhost:11434 only when the var is truly unset).
#   OLLAMA_HOST=http://host.docker.internal:11434
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# OpenAI-compatible providers (no native langchain prefix): required when the
# selected model uses a cursor:/openrouter:/lmstudio: spec. LM Studio is keyless.
# Examples:
#   CURSOR_BASE_URL=https://api.cursor.sh/v1
#   OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
#   LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
CURSOR_BASE_URL=
OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=
LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=


# Default model for the system (must match an installed langchain provider package).
#
# LEAVE THIS UNSET unless you want to pin a model. Unset means auto-selection
# runs, which now lands on a LOCAL Ollama model (ollama is priority 0) -- local
# models have no free-tier rate limit, so tests and smoke runs can make real
# model calls instead of skipping them. Setting it here is not free: env outranks
# the profile file in the config chain (harness/config.py), so a value here
# silently shadows whatever `harness config` wrote, and the wizard's model choice
# stops taking effect with no warning.
#
# Set it only to override that -- a cloud model, or a local tag other than the
# provider's default. Use whatever `ollama list` shows on your host; a tag with no
# matching providers/ollama/models/<tag>.toml still runs, it just carries no metadata.
#   DEEPAGENTS_MODEL=openai:gpt-4o
#   DEEPAGENTS_MODEL=ollama:gemma4:harnesstest1
DEEPAGENTS_MODEL=

DEEPAGENTS_TASK=

# Present thread id (the live, auto-loaded conversation). Unset => a FRESH thread
# per run (`session-<ts>`), so a new session never silently resumes yesterday's
# conversation (Milestone 2 §2.1). Set this to a prior id to RESUME that named
# thread (state persists in <workspace>/.deepagents/checkpoints.sqlite). Leave it
# commented out for the fresh-by-default behavior — an empty value would pin the
# empty id, not "fresh".
#   DEEPAGENTS_THREAD_ID=my-refactor

# --- Past archive (Milestone 2) ---------------------------------------------
# Every session is also appended to a SEPARATE store the checkpointer can't see
# (<workspace>/.deepagents/past.sqlite), read back only via /recall or the
# recall_past tool — never auto-injected. Set to 0 to disable archiving entirely.
DEEPAGENTS_ARCHIVE=1

# Continual-topic label for this run (§2.4). Tags the session's archive row and
# scopes recall to that lane by default (/recall --all widens). Unset => untagged,
# recall stays global. Also settable mid-session with the /topic REPL command.
DEEPAGENTS_TOPIC=

# Directory inside the container exposed to the coding agent.
# Must match the run-docker volume mount (/project/workspace). Do not change unless you remount.
AGENT_WORKSPACE=/project/workspace

# Extra env vars to expose to the agent's shell tool. The shell env is an
# allowlist (PATH/HOME/CONDA_*/GIT_*/locale + common shell vars); everything
# else — including credentials — is withheld. Add your own as a comma/space list;
# a trailing '*' is a prefix. A bare name is passed through even if it looks like
# a secret (naming it is explicit opt-in); a '*' prefix still withholds secrets.
#   DEEPAGENTS_SHELL_ENV_ALLOW=MYAPP_URL, MYAPP_*
DEEPAGENTS_SHELL_ENV_ALLOW=

# --- Cost / token / energy tracker (Milestone 1) ----------------------------
# Optional per-session ceilings: the REPL ends loudly once a cumulative total is
# crossed (after the current model call). Unset = no ceiling. CLI --max-cost /
# --max-tokens override these.
DEEPAGENTS_MAX_COST=
DEEPAGENTS_MAX_TOKENS=

# Fallback price for models with NO [pricing] table, in USD per MILLION tokens.
# Unset => such models warn ONCE then run with cost shown as a floor (unpriced
# calls excluded); set this to estimate their cost instead of omitting it.
DEEPAGENTS_PRICE_ESTIMATE=

# Electricity price in USD per kWh. When set, the tracker converts estimated
# energy (Wh) into an electricity cost on the usage line. Unset => energy only.
DEEPAGENTS_ELECTRICITY_RATE=

# Optional tracing. If LANGSMITH_TRACING is true but LANGSMITH_API_KEY is empty,
# the harness flags the missing key and disables tracing for the run (it never
# attempts to connect keyless).
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=
LANGSMITH_TRACING=false
LANGSMITH_PROJECT=

# Auth provider (optional, uncomment for [auth])
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_DEFAULT_KEY=
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

# Frontend (optional, uncomment for [frontend] + matching [auth])
# Clerk only — browser-facing publishable key. Supabase reuses the keys above.
# CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# --- Workspace visibility / secret masking (Milestone 4) --------------------
# When on (default 1), the harness scans the workspace before launching the agent
# and mounts empty overlays over the paths matched by the mask policy (pattern
# defaults + .agentignore + designated-secret floor). Set to 0 to disable the
# scan and mask entirely (byte-for-byte Milestone 3 behaviour).
DEEPAGENTS_MASK=1

# Mask mode: deny (default) — see everything but masked paths are present-but-empty.
# allow — only allow-listed paths and the agent-writable area are visible.
# Can also be set per-workspace via the #!mode: header directive in .agentignore.
# DEEPAGENTS_MASK_MODE=deny

# Override the in-workspace config filename (default .agentignore). The state-dir
# authoritative config is unaffected.
# DEEPAGENTS_AGENTIGNORE=

# --- bwrap fs jail (Milestone 4 slice H) — OFF by default -------------------
# 1 re-execs the harness into a bubblewrap mount namespace, so every tool (the
# in-process file tools AND the shell) is bounded by one bind whitelist. This
# gives the designated-secret floor an enforcer independent of the docker mask,
# and stops the shell tool reaching <state-dir>/denials.jsonl by absolute path.
#
# Off by default on purpose: it requires relaxing the container's seccomp filter
# (Docker's default blocks unprivileged user namespaces). run-docker passes the
# vendored narrow profile automatically — Docker's default plus exactly
# clone/unshare/mount/umount2/pivot_root — and refuses to launch if it is missing
# rather than running unjailed. That relaxation grants no privilege but does
# expose kernel user-namespace surface, so turning it on is a deliberate trade.
# See deepagent-image/seccomp/README.md.
# DEEPAGENTS_JAIL=1
#
# AppArmor stance for the jail. Read by run-docker on the HOST (it only affects
# docker run flags; nothing in the container reads it).
#
# seccomp is only ONE of the two gates. On Ubuntu/Debian Docker, Docker also
# applies a `docker-default` AppArmor profile whose literal `deny mount,` blocks
# bwrap at its first mount — after `unshare` has already succeeded — and no
# seccomp change affects that. Leave this unset and the harness fails CLOSED at
# startup with a diagnostic naming AppArmor, rather than running unjailed.
#
# `unconfined` makes the jail work on such a host, at the cost of dropping the
# WHOLE profile (the /proc and /sys write denials and the ptrace peer restriction),
# not just its deny-mount rule — a wider trade than DEEPAGENTS_JAIL alone. Any
# other value is treated as the name of a profile already loaded on the host.
# Nothing is needed on Docker Desktop/WSL2, which loads no AppArmor policy.
# The real fix is slice J — see docs/milestones/in-progress/milestone4.md §11.6.
# DEEPAGENTS_JAIL_APPARMOR=unconfined


